      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(mattermost): reject oversized websocket events",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators connected to a buggy or hostile self-hosted Mattermost server could have the monitor WebSocket client buffer an oversized event payload before the `ws` client rejected it.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Mattermost monitor now sets a 4 MiB inbound WebSocket payload cap on the default `ws` client. Mattermost WebSocket traffic is documented as JSON event envelopes, and Mattermost server source permits large post props/cards, so this stays above a valid posted-event envelope while avoiding the upstream `ws` client default of 100 MiB for this monitor path.\n\nMattermost API docs: https://developers.mattermost.com/api-documentation/\n\nMattermost post validation source: https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/blob/master/server/public/model/post.go\n\n## User Impact\n\nMattermost users keep receiving normal channel activity, while runaway or hostile WebSocket frames fail fast with standard payload-too-large behavior instead of being buffered up to the much larger client default.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/mattermost/src/mattermost/monitor-websocket.test.ts`: 11 tests passed.\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 extensions/mattermost/src/mattermost/monitor-websocket.ts extensions/mattermost/src/mattermost/monitor-websocket.test.ts`: passed.\n- `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs --tsconfig tsconfig.json extensions/mattermost/src/mattermost/monitor-websocket.ts extensions/mattermost/src/mattermost/monitor-websocket.test.ts`: passed.\n- `git diff --check origin/main..HEAD`: passed.\n\nLoopback proof using `createMattermostConnectOnce()` with the production default socket factory:\n\n```text\nconfigured_max_payload_bytes=4194304\nmattermost_props_json_runes=760023\nnormal_frame_bytes=100\nlarge_valid_frame_bytes=1520150\noversized_frame_bytes=4194305\nlarge_valid_event_received=yes\nclient_error=mattermost websocket error: RangeError: Max payload size exceeded\nserver_close_code=1009\nreceived_posts=normal-post,large-post\n```\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex\n",
        "branch": "sunlit/fix/mattermost-ws-max-payload",
